second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What is the population of Blue Lake Township, Michigan?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0033-50ae3c8b559b:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 115, \"text\": \"Blue Lake Township, Kalkaska County, Michigan Blue Lake Township is a civil township of Kalkaska County in the U.S.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0033-50ae3c8b559b:d00\", \"start\": 116, \"end\": 134, \"text\": \"state of Michigan.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0033-50ae3c8b559b:d00\", \"start\": 135, \"end\": 190, \"text\": \"As of the 2000 census, the township population was 428.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0033-50ae3c8b559b:d00\", \"start\": 191, \"end\": 394, \"text\": \"According to the United States Census Bureau, the township has a total area of 36.2 square miles (93.8 km²), of which 34.7 square miles (89.7 km²) is land and 1.6 square miles (4.1 km²) (4.36%) is water.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0033-50ae3c8b559b:d00\", \"start\": 395, \"end\": 502, \"text\": \"As of the census of 2000, there were 428 people, 202 households, and 150 families residing in the township.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0033-50ae3c8b559b:d00\", \"start\": 503, \"end\": 561, \"text\": \"The population density was 12.4 per square mile (4.8/km²).\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0033-50ae3c8b559b:d00\", \"start\": 562, \"end\": 576, \"text\": \"There were 738\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0033-50ae3c8b559b:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 198, \"text\": \"1930 3,799 −31.9 % 1940 5,159 35.8 % 1950 4,597 −10.9 % 1960 4,382 −4.7 % 1970 5,272 20.3 % 1980 10,952 107.7 % 1990 13,497 23.2 % 2000 16,571 22.8 % 2010 17,153 3.5 % 2020 17,939 4.6 % 2023 ( est .\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0033-50ae3c8b559b:d01\", \"start\": 199, \"end\": 444, \"text\": \") 18,490 [ 12 ] 3.1 % US Decennial Census [ 13 ] 1790-1960 [ 14 ] 1900-1990 [ 15 ] 1990-2000 [ 16 ] 2010-2018 [ 2 ] At the 2010 United States census [ 17 ] there were 16,571 people , 6,428 households , and 4,634 families residing in the county .\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0033-50ae3c8b559b:d01\", \"start\": 445, \"end\": 459, \"text\": \"The population\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0033-50ae3c8b559b:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 49, \"text\": \"Blue Lake Township , Kalkaska County , Michigan .\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0033-50ae3c8b559b:d02\", \"start\": 50, \"end\": 504, \"text\": \"Township in Michigan , United States Blue Lake Township , Michigan Township Blue Lake Township Show map of Michigan Blue Lake Township Show map of the United States Coordinates : 43°25′42″N 86°13′08″W ﻿ / ﻿ 43.42833°N 86.21889°W ﻿ / 43.42833 ; -86.21889 Country United States State Michigan County Muskegon Area [ 1 ] • Total 35.74 sq mi ( 92.6 km 2 ) • Land 33.56 sq mi ( 86.9 km 2 ) • Water 2.18 sq mi ( 5.6 km 2 ) Elevation 604 ft ( 184 m ) Population\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0033-50ae3c8b559b:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 199, \"text\": \"1930 3,799 −31.9 % 1940 5,159 35.8 % 1950 4,597 −10.9 % 1960 4,382 −4.7 % 1970 5,272 20.3 % 1980 10,952 107.7 % 1990 13,497 23.2 % 2000 16,571 22.8 % 2010 42,800 158.3 % 2020 44,939 5.0 % 2023 ( est.\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0033-50ae3c8b559b:d03\", \"start\": 200, \"end\": 285, \"text\": \") 45,490 [ 12 ] 1.2 % US Decennial Census [ 13 ] 1790-1960 [ 14 ] 1900-1990 [ 15 ] 19\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0033-50ae3c8b559